1 AVAILABLE POSITION

San Mauro Torinese (TO) - SpacePark

HYBRID

Argotec is an Italian aerospace company specializing in the production of small satellite platforms (from 6U Cubesats up to 250kg-platforms) and innovative products to improve the comfort of space explorers. Thanks to its facilities and know-how, the company's activities follow the "all in-house" concept, which includes design, development, integration, qualification, and operational services. At Argotec, we’re not just building satellites; we’re shaping the future of space innovation.

To support our Company’s growth, we are looking an AIT Engineer - Harness Designer, who will be part of our Engineering AIT Unit, focusing on the design and development of harnesses for our satellite platforms and ground support equipment. The ideal candidate has a solid electronics background and an interest in cable and harness design, from schematics to material selection.

We foster a collaborative environment where every Argonaut can contribute with their ideas and expertise, create meaningful value together, and transform feedback and mistakes into opportunities for learning and innovation, growing both professionally and personally, as individuals and as a team.

DUTIES

As an AIT Engineer, you will be responsible for the design, documentation, assembly, and testing of harnesses for both our flight and test projects.

The activities will include (but are not limited to):

- Design of electrical harnesses, including schematics, layout diagrams and pin-to-pin lists;
- Selection of connectors, contacts, wires and other parts based on electrical, mechanical and environmental requirements;
- Analysis of technical documentation and manufacturing specifications;
- Support to harness manufacturing and assembly;
- Drafting of technical documentation, including design files, assembly procedures, and test procedures and reports;
- Testing and validation of cables and harnesses, including activities in Clean Room;
- Directly interface with internal and external stakeholders for harness definition and manufacturing;
- Support with QA/PA processes definition and non-conformances management;
- Harness routing definition in accordance with satellite’s mechanical design;
- Support to broader AIT activities (PCBs debug, test setups, small assemblies) when needed;
- Ensuring compliance with workplace safety regulations and procedures

GENERAL REQUIREMENTS

- Bachelor’s or Master’s Degree in Electronics, Electrical Engineering, or a related technical field. Technical High School Diploma will also be considered;
- At least 3 years of experience in a similar role;
- Good written and oral communication skills in English;
- Strong analytical and problem-solving mindset;
- Proactive attitude, attention to detail and willingness to continuously learn;
- Ability to collaborate effectively within cross-functional teams and manage priorities in a dynamic environment.

REQUIRED EXPERIENCE & SKILLS

- Proven ability to read electrical schematics and wiring diagrams;
- Basic knowledge of harness design fundamentals (materials, design rules, etc.);
- Experience in soldering through-hole and SMD parts and cables;
- Good familiarity with laboratory instruments (multimeter, power supply, etc.) and tools (crimp pliers, wire strippers, wire cutters, etc.).
- Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple activities with precision;
- High level of reliability, proactivity and accountability;
- Flexibility and adaptability in a dynamic and fast-paced environment;
- Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities simultaneously, working under tight deadlines.

ADDITIONAL ASSETS

- Previous experience in the aerospace or defense industry will be considered a plus;
- Familiarity with CAD tools for electronics or harness design (Altium preferred) and mechanical design (Solidworks preferred);
- Experience in ESD controlled environments;
- Knowledge of ECSS and IPC standards.

WHY JOIN ARGOTEC?

- Opportunity to work with highly motivated colleagues in a very innovative environment;
- Professional training and career development opportunities;
- Flexible working time schedule and a hybrid work policy;
- Monthly "Free-Day" - every second Friday: time off to dedicate to your family and/or hobbies;
- A diversified community that organizes extra-work and fun activities;
- Salary range: 30.000€ to 35.000€

The Company reserves the right to assess the appropriate job level and compensation package based on objective criteria emerging throughout the selection process. These evaluations will be carried out in alignment with the candidate's seniority, skills, and experience, as well as with the scope and responsibilities of the role. Any compensation proposal will be defined in compliance with the principles of fairness, transparency, and equal opportunity, in accordance with applicable regulations.

Our selection process is tailored to each role and includes at least a call with our Talent Acquisition Team, a technical evaluation, and a final in-person meeting. Your recruiter will share more insights during your first meeting with us!

At Argotec, we thrive on diverse perspectives and unique strengths. Your individuality could be the missing piece to our puzzle! Even if you don't meet every skill listed above, we encourage you to apply if you're passionate about the role and believe you can contribute to our team's success.

Our selection process is built on impartiality, transparency, and equal opportunity, ensuring that every candidate is evaluated based on skills, experience, and potential. As part of our commitment to inclusivity, we actively encourage applications from individuals belonging to protected categories (Law 68/99).

At Argotec, we’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and inclusion, welcoming individuals of all backgrounds. This opportunity is open to everyone, regardless – for instance – of ethnic or cultural background, color, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, or national origin.

Join us in a workplace where everyone belongs.

This announcement is aimed at both sexes, under laws 903/77 and 125/91, and to people of all ages and all nationalities, under legislative decrees 215/03 and 216/03.

1 AVAILABLE POSITION

San Mauro Torinese (TO) - SpacePark

HYBRID

Argotec is an Italian aerospace company specializing in the production of small satellite platforms (from 6U Cubesats up to 250kg+ platforms). Thanks to its facilities and know-how, the company's activities follow the "all in-house" concept, which includes design, development, integration, qualification, and operational services. At Argotec, we’re not just building satellites; we’re shaping the future of space innovation.

To support our Company’s growth, we are looking for a Defence Solutions Architect to join our Defence Team that will play a key part in the definition and development of complex satellite systems, with focus on dual-use and military applications, contributing to strategic programs at both national and international level.

You will combine your engineering background in space systems with strategic vision, technical leadership and the ability to engage effectively with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders. You will interact closely with customers, partners, press and internal teams, translating complex technical concepts and data into clear, compelling solutions and narratives that support decision-making and programme success.

The role requires availability to periodic business travel (approximately 25%) in order to support customer interactions, programs execution and representation at key defence and space industry events.

We foster a collaborative environment where every Argonaut can contribute with their ideas and expertise, create meaningful value together, and transform feedback and mistakes into opportunities for learning and innovation, growing both professionally and personally, as individuals and as a team.

DUTIES

As a Defence Solutions Architect directly reporting to Argotec's Executive Director Defence Business, you will contribute to the conceptualization and development of state-of-the-art spaceborne Defence solutions according to the company vision, strategy, and roadmaps. You will create and present innovative space systems to key clients, internal management and stakeholders.

The activities will include (but are not limited to):

- Trade-off complex technical solutions, develop mission concepts and architectures, and support complex bid and proposal processes;
- Actively contribute to the definition and evolution of Argotec’s Defence strategy, supporting the identification of new opportunities, capabilities, and market positioning in dual-use and military domains;
- Collaborate closely with cross-functional teams, including Product Management, Marketing, Sales, Engineering and R&D to ensure cohesive product strategies, developments and launches;
- Build strong relationships with key stakeholders, both internal and external including customers, partners and institutional entities, acting as a trusted technical and strategic reference;
- Continuously monitor market trends and customer feedback translating insights into actionable inputs to refine and adjust the Defence portfolio and strategy;
- Act as an evangelist for Argotec’s products and solutions, representing its Defence offerings;
- Participate in industry events and engage with customers to build relationships and gather valuable insights;
- Define Defence product and system requirements, assist the planning of product design and support full development lifecycle;
- Support product-related publications, presentations and contributions at relevant conferences, workshops and defence-oriented events.

GENERAL REQUIREMENTS

- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Engineering, Business or related fields;
- At least 8 years of experience in Product Management, Systems Engineering, R&D in new-space sector;
- Analytical thinking and proactive problem-solving attitude;
- Excellent communication skills and ability to collaborate with cross-functional teams;
- Proactive and autonomous approach, combined with a strong sense of ownership and accountability;
- Ability to obtain Italian security clearances;
- Ability to translate a strategic vision in concrete projects;
- Excellent written and oral communication in English.

REQUIRED EXPERIENCES & SKILLS

- Solid understanding of New Space products and end-to-end solution development cycles, covering the full lifecycle from concept definition and system architecture to market delivery and operational deployment;
- Wide expertise in modern Defence needs and state-of-the-art systems, with focus on space and air domains;
- Strong knowledge of the aerospace industry, particularly in the small satellite (SmallSat) segment, including platforms, subsystems and mission architectures;
- Experience in conducting market research, user research and data analysis;
- Ability to work autonomously in a fast-paced and dynamic environment, managing complexity and ambiguity while maintaining a high level of technical and strategic rigor;
- Strong adaptability to changing priorities and evolving requirements, with the capability to effectively balance technical depth, business needs and stakeholder expectations;
- Demonstrated ability to establish and sustain long-term professional relationships with government, civilian, and military stakeholders, acting as a trusted technical and strategic counterpart.

ADDITIONAL ASSETS

- Established network in the Defense & Aerospace industry;
- Previous experience in the Defence & Aerospace sector;
- Knowledge of space standards (CCSDS, ECSS, MIL etc.);
- Strong business acumen and financial awareness;
- Continuous learning attitude and intellectual curiosity, particularly towards emerging Defence, space and dual-use technologies.

WHY JOIN ARGOTEC?

- Opportunity to work with highly motivated colleagues in a very innovative environment.
- Professional training and career development opportunities.
- Flexible working time schedule and a hybrid work policy.
- Monthly "Free-Day" - every second Friday: time off to dedicate to your family and/or hobbies.
- A diversified community that organizes extra-work and fun activities;
- Salary range: from 50.000€ to 60.000€

The Company reserves the right to assess the appropriate job level and compensation package based on objective criteria emerging throughout the selection process. These evaluations will be carried out in alignment with the candidate’s seniority, skills, and experience, as well as with the scope and responsibilities of the role. Any compensation proposal will be defined in compliance with the principles of fairness, transparency, and equal opportunity, in accordance with applicable regulations.

